7 #edb/ref 17592186050613 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152272 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186152608 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152272 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186152667 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152272 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186498523 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152272 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186498528 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152272 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186559811 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152272 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186559849 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152272 #edb/ref 1039 "Solving for an Unknown Amount" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152272 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186151826 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152272 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "3f29a835-91e3-51e3-a016-e13d296b7654" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152312 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186153254 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152312 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186153255 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152312 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186153256 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152312 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186153257 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152312 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152312 #edb/ref 1045 "Understanding Proportional Relationships From Descriptions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152312 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186153254 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152312 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049141 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152312 #edb/ref 1050 480.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152312 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "a59e2561-e0dc-5240-8024-effab456d18a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152666 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186150503 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152666 #edb/ref 1069 "q-68126" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152666 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152666 #edb/ref 1071 "Jordan wants to paint the outside of his home. Using $2$ gallons of paint, he was able to paint $450$ square feet of the surface. There is a proportional relationship between the volume of paint $x$ (in gallons) that Jordan uses and the area $y$ (in square feet) he paints. What is the equation that represents the relationship between $x$ and $y?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152666 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2352802a-045d-530a-8500-09dde40a2d51" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152666 #edb/ref 1074 "Every proportional relationship takes the form $y=kx,$ where $k$ is the constant of proportionality.\n\nWe are told that Jordan painted $y=450$ square feet using $x=2$ gallons of paint.\n\nWe can find the constant of proportionality by computing the ratio of the $y$-value to the $x$-value, as follows:\n\n$$\nk=\\frac{y}{x}=\\frac{450}{2}=225\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation is\n\n$$\ny=225x.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153254 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186153255 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153254 #edb/ref 1061 54183 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153254 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "d67d1aae-88f2-5c83-9e8b-9cb74a319475" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153254 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186153437 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153255 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186153256 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153255 #edb/ref 1061 54184 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153255 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "2b45a9cd-8289-51d2-8e4f-c06b2b089b8c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153255 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186152270 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153256 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186153257 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153256 #edb/ref 1061 54187 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153256 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "db6fedfb-85d0-5eb6-a2b9-f9df621ac942" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153256 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186152271 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153257 #edb/ref 1061 54190 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153257 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "8a87b9ba-c67e-5da1-b438-76dadef85d15" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153257 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186152272 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153437 #edb/ref 1064 "Recall that two variables, $x$ and $y,$ are said to have a proportional relationship if their ratio is constant. The constant of proportionality $k$ is given by\n\n$$\nk = \\dfrac{y}{x}.\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the equation above as follows:\n\n$$\ny = kx\n$$\n\nThe following statements are all equivalent:\n\n- $y = kx$\n\n- $y$ **varies directly** with $x$\n\n- $y$ is **directly proportional** to $x$\n\n- $y \\propto x$\n\nProportional relationships frequently occur in real-world problems. Let's see an example." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153437 #edb/ref 1065 8191 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153437 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "cd20b689-18a3-54cb-97a9-7fa52d610ec1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153437 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559008 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186559921 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559008 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186559929 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559008 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186559970 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559008 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559008 #edb/ref 1045 "Understanding Proportional Relationships From Descriptions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559008 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186559921 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559008 #edb/ref 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046647 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559008 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049141 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559008 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "a6fc1838-76b5-5520-9919-4902b4fe7101" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559032 #edb/ref 1080 "-31" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559032 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559032 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "084c23f6-d996-50e5-a433-1f7029a87dd6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559055 #edb/ref 1080 "y=900x" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559055 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559055 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "10370